<title>USA: Dime declines comment on stock activity.</title>
<headline>Dime declines comment on stock activity.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dime Bancorp Inc declined on Friday to comment on a rise in its stock to a 52-week high.</p>
<p>&quot;We never comment&quot; on such matters, a Dime spokesman said when asked if the activity could be tied to a recent published report that the thrift was a merger candidate.</p>
<p>The stock rose 1-3/8 to 16-1/2 on volume of about 3.8 million shares.</p>
<p>Traders in the options pits said activity picked up Thursday and Friday, especially in Dime calls.  </p>
<p>At Republic New York Corp, which has been mentioned as a possible suitor for Dime, a spokesman said, &quot;we don't comment on rumors.&quot;</p>
<p>Republic was up 5/8 to 78-3/4.</p>
